## Honest patterns
- "Architecture decisions stay onshore. Implementation is global. Quality gates are shared."
- "We don't follow the sun for thinking. We follow the sun for execution behind a clear contract."
- "Distributed pods need a typed interface boundary, just like services do."

## Anti-patterns
- Do not pitch "lower cost" as the value. Pitch consistency, throughput, and timezone resilience.
- Do not promise "seamless" handoffs. Name the artifact and the cadence.
- Do not collapse engineering culture into process. Name what onshore owns vs what offshore owns.

